{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-24 10:33:59 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-24 17:33:59 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nVerdict: request changes.\n\nP1 | [src/cljc/dao/jing/mem.cljc:104](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/mem.cljc:104) | The public handle exposes `:state`, whose content now contains mutable host byte arrays. A reproduction mutated stored `[1 2]` into `[1 3]`; `mem/entries` returned the forged value while `jing/get` detected an integrity error. `entries` also decodes without address verification at line 118. | Keep the atom inaccessible, expose a closure-based snapshot view, and use `segment-value` for verified decoding. Add mutation-isolation tests for both input and exposed state/output.\n\nP1 | [src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:457](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:457) | The required shared byte-store boundary was not implemented. `segment-key` encodes once, then `materialize!` passes the original value to the backend; memory and file encode it again at [mem.cljc:38](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/mem.cljc:38) and [file.cljc:344](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc:344). Instrumentation confirmed two encoder calls for one insertion, contrary to the encode-once contract at [dao.jing.cbor.md:98](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:98). | Encode once in the Jing wrapper, derive the address from those bytes, and delegate through `:put-bytes-fn`/`:get-bytes-fn`; keep public APIs value-facing.\n\nP2 | [docs/design/dao.jing.md:190](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.jing.md:190) | The authoritative design still declares the order-normalized printer current, lists it as an open item at line 486, and describes file records as `[address payload]` at line 407. This contradicts the implemented clean break. | Replace the transitional-printer sections with the canonical-CBOR and byte-store contracts